  "title": "Building the agent was never the hard part: the build-vs-buy conundrum",
  "summary": "The foundation models work great and will keep getting better. So why do most agent projects in financial services still fail? And fail in the same, predictable way? For those who have tried, it becomes quickly apparent that there’s a vast distance between a demo that impresses a room and a system an institution can rely on, at production volume, inside its own controls. That distance is where the build-versus-buy conundrum is almost always underestimated.",
